WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.500
Here's a week of booking reminders at a made-up dog groomer. Every message you'll see is the real output of the code.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.950
Monday morning, Jordan books a full groom online.

3
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.680
A confirmation goes out at once, with a link to move or cancel.

4
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.740
Ana books late that night,

5
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.560
and the confirmation goes straight away. Ana just booked, after all.

6
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.520
The day before Jordan's appointment, a reminder.

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.350
Then Jordan moves to Thursday. A new confirmation goes out, and the old reminders are dropped.

8
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.150
On Wednesday, each of them gets a reminder the day before.

9
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.340
Thursday morning, the owner gets the day's schedule.

10
00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:58.580
Ana's two-hour reminder would land at seven in the morning, so it's skipped.

11
00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.890
And two hours before, Jordan gets a last reminder.

12
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:10.140
Online booking and reminders is four hundred dollars, fixed, set up in the booking tool you already use.
